WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:01.680
<b>Dorry and Brogy</b>

3
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.910
[gasps]

4
00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.980
[BOTH gasp]

5
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.080
[LUFFY grunts]

6
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.450
[VIVI]
What's the matter?

7
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.820
[sighs]

8
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.890
This fight. It's...wow!

9
00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.090
[rumbling]

10
00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.000
[DORRY, BROGY yell]

11
00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.470
[growls]

12
00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.110
[rumbling, thudding]

13
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.180
[DORRY, BROGY growling]

14
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.520
[DORRY growls]

15
00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.490
[BROGY yells]

16
00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.030
[yells]

17
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.530
[yelling]

18
00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.170
[BOTH yelling]

19
00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.980
[whimpers]

20
00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.810
He...

21
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.340
He blocked that hit
with his helmet.

22
00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.540
That's incredible!

23
00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.010
A couple of inches left or right
and it would've killed him!

24
00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.350
[BROGY growls]

25
00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:24.300
[DORRY, BROGY grunting]

26
00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.670
What an incredible fight, huh?

27
00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.930
Every one of those
attacks is aimed

28
00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.330
at some vital spot.

29
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.340
Just one slip from either
of them, and that's it...

30
00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.540
they're dead!

31
00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.410
[NAMI]
These guys have really
been fighting to the death

32
00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.540
for 100 years?
That's gotta get old.

33
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.320
This is a good thing.

34
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.260
This is our chance
to get away. Let's go.

35
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.010
[NAMI]
Usopp?

36
00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.830
Amazing...

37
00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.640
[BROGY]
Why?

38
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.770
I don't remember!

39
00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:10.080
[BROGY laughs]

40
00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.900
They fight so seriously...

41
00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.130
And they don't even know why.

42
00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.270
This fight's getting
really annoying.

43
00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.940
[USOPP]
Don't you see?!

44
00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:24.450
This is an example

45
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.770
of a real battle
between real men.

46
00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.010
Say what?

47
00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.580
[USOPP]
Maybe an analogy will help.

48
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.950
It's as if they have each
planted a flag in their hearts

49
00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.090
that says, "I am a warrior."

50
00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.190
This flag is more
important than anything,

51
00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.390
more than their lives, even.

52
00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.590
They can never allow the flag

53
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.460
to be destroyed by someone else.

54
00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.130
That's why they've both
continued this fight

55
00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.130
for 100 years.

56
00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:51.070
[DORRY, BROGY yell]

57
00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.270
[USOPP]
Do you see it now?
This is a proud duel...

58
00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:59.740
a legendary fight...between
two dedicated warriors.

59
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:00.700
Yeah, whatever.

60
00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.310
That warrior stuff
doesn't really interest me

61
00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.710
in the slightest.

62
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.850
You coming?

63
00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.080
[USOPP]
No, I'm still watching this.

64
00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.720
This is my ultimate goal.

65
00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.820
This right here.

66
00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.060
To be a brave warrior
like each of these titans.

67
00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.260
Really, though, someday...

68
00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.000
...I will be a proud
warrior of the sea!

69
00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.020
[NAMI]
So what you're saying then,

70
00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.010
is that you wanna be a giant?

71
00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.210
[USOPP]
Huh?

72
00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.360
Moron! You haven't
listened to a single word

73
00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.330
I've said, have you?

74
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.530
Hey, Usopp...

75
00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.670
Isn't there something that
you're supposed to be watching?

76
00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:41.850
[DORRY, BROGY grunting]

77
00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.650
If there's a village full of
warriors like these two,

78
00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.190
then I really wanna
go there someday!

79
00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.950
[rumbling]

80
00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.450
[DORRY, BROGY groan]

81
00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.490
[panting]

82
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.580
It's safe to say...

83
00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.470
...that we're both starting to
get homesick here... huh, Dorry?

84
00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:12.070
That's why I intend to
end this duel of ours.

85
00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.010
I'm going to beat you
and go home to Elbaph.

86
00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.580
Got that, Brogy?

87
00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:26.190
[yells]

88
00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.360
Seventy-three thousand...

89
00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.660
...four hundred sixty-six duels.

90
00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.960
Seventy-three thousand,

91
00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.800
four hundred and
sixty-six draws.

92
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.070
[rumbling]

93
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.490
Hey, if you're done...

94
00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.850
Get out of the way.

95
00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.490
Wait... I can handle this.

96
00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.690
[roars]

97
00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:16.660
[MISS VALENTINE giggles]

98
00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.730
[MISS VALENTINE]
Ten Thousand Kilogram Press!

99
00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:34.580
[Mr. 3]
Oh, hello, Mr. 5.

100
00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:37.680
[MR. 5]
I'm impressed by the décor.

101
00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.260
You have a talent for
turnin' even the most

102
00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.380
savage environment into a home.

103
00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.960
I admire you, which is
why I feel compelled

104
00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.020
to remind both of you:

105
00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.790
This mission belongs
to me and Miss Valentine.

106
00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.760
Rest assured we won't slip up
like we did last time.

107
00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.330
[MR. 3]
Slip up?

108
00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.770
That's not why I'm here...

109
00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.720
Mr. 5, Miss Valentine...
the simple fact of the matter is

110
00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.650
you are both weak.

111
00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.320
[MR. 3]
Don't waste your energy pouting.

112
00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.200
It is what it is.
Take a look at this.

113
00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.230
I'd like to thank you both

114
00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:10.170
for affording me an excuse
to come to this island.

115
00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.820
I'll enjoy the opportunity
to hunt some truly...

116
00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.420
...big game.

117
00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:15.920
[MR. 3 chuckles]

118
00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.540
Dorry the Blue Ogre and Brogy

119
00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:20.860
the Red Ogre of the
Giant Warrior Pirates.

120
00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.960
Everyone's heard of them.

121
00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:22.830
It's ancient legend.

122
00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.360
Hey, this poster is
over 100 years old!

123
00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.700
Well, those two legends
are alive and well

124
00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.050
on this very island...
battling over a century now.

125
00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.290
Back when that poster was new,

126
00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.460
the bounty on their heads was
100,000,000 berries apiece...

127
00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.460
200,000,000 for
the both of them.

128
00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.480
[MR. 5]
Two hundred million berries

129
00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.630
is an impressive sum.

130
00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:42.280
But that doesn't change
the fact that they're giants.

131
00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.380
There's a wise saying...

132
00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.800
Superior criminals are those
who execute their crimes

133
00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:48.280
using superior intellect.

134
00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.520
All you have to do is follow
my precise instructions.

135
00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:52.400
With a smidgeon of forethought

136
00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.420
and perseverance,
we can find the solution

137
00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:57.850
to even the most
gargantuan of obstacles.

138
00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.320
[DORRY chuckles]

139
00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.460
[BROGY chuckles]

140
00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:18.460
[DORRY, BROGY laughing]

141
00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.300
Hey, Dorry.

142
00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.840
A couple guests of mine
gave me some alcohol.

143
00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.720
Drinks? It's been a long while,

144
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.810
eh, Brogy?

145
00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:30.410
[laughs]

146
00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:36.420
[BROGY, DORRY laughing]

147
00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.860
That's interesting...
so Brogy's guests

148
00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.830
are friends of yours, then?
I saw a goofy-looking guy

149
00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.030
with a long nose
and a woman there.

150
00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.600
That's Usopp and Nami.

151
00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.700
They said they weren't even
gonna get off the ship.

152
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.610
I guess they wanted to have
an adventure after all.

153
00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.740
If they're your
friends, then I guess

154
00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.880
I can thank you, too,
for these yummy refreshments.

155
00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.830
So, Dorry, tell us...

156
00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:03.030
Does it really take a year for
the log to reset on this island?

157
00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.160
Yes.

158
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.470
Didn't you notice all the
mounds of human skeletons

159
00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:10.500
that are lying around here?
I guess it's hard not to.

160
00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.500
The people who come
to this island tend to die

161
00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.470
before their logs are reset.

162
00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.390
Some become dinosaur food,

163
00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.580
some die from heat or
thirst or starvation.

164
00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.080
Others are killed because
they stupidly attack us.

165
00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.080
Whatever the case,
they all die here somehow.

166
00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.070
An entire year on
this island just seems

167
00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.630
to be too long. So far,
no humans have been able

168
00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.990
to survive here
for the full year.

169
00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.690
[VIVI]
What are we going to do?

170
00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.480
Even if we could manage
to last here for a year,

171
00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.150
who knows what could
happen by then?

172
00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.690
My country could be lost.

173
00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.090
She's right.

174
00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:45.520
Plus, I'd get bored
here after a year.

175
00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:48.160
Isn't there anything else
we can do about it, old man?

176
00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.110
[DORRY]
Hm... We do have
an eternal pose here,

177
00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:54.450
but it's magnetic link is
to our home village, Elbaph.

178
00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.510
Basically, that eternal pose
is what Brogy and I

179
00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.150
have been fighting for with
our duels this whole time.

180
00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:02.790
Of course, you can try
to take it by force.

181
00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.590
No, that's not gonna work.

182
00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.960
Elbaph isn't the place that
we're trying to get to.

183
00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.800
We just wanna get to the island
that's right after this one.

184
00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:10.660
Right?

185
00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.060
[VIVI]
Yes.

186
00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.880
We must stay on the route
that's going to lead us

187
00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.650
to my home, or else
there's no point.

188
00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.980
Yeah.

189
00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:21.620
Maybe you can try
sailing forward randomly.

190
00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.160
You may get there eventually,

191
00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.140
if you're real lucky.

192
00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:32.840
[LUFFY laughs]

193
00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.470
Maybe so.

194
00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.680
[laughs]

195
00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.810
[LUFFY]
We may actually get there!

196
00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.760
[laughs]

197
00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.220
[DORRY]
Now that I think
about it, someone did

198
00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.040
leave the island once
before his log was reset.

199
00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.440
[LUFFY]
And what happened to him?

200
00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.190
[DORRY]
How should I know that?

201
00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.730
[LUFFY]
I'm sure he was able
to get to the next island.

202
00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:53.910
[DORRY]
That must be it!

203
00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:58.110
[DORRY, LUFFY laughing]

204
00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.950
[VIVI]
What is so funny?

205
00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:06.890
[DORRY, LUFFY laughing]

206
00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:07.900
[VIVI]
I don't understand
what these two idiots

207
00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.240
are laughing about
at a time like this!

208
00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.470
[BROGY]
A brave warrior
of the seas, you said?

209
00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:20.470
What's that exactly?

210
00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.500
I'm talking about you guys!

211
00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:25.710
What I really want is to be
like the two of you someday!

212
00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:27.730
Huh? You wanna be a giant?

213
00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:29.350
[NAMI]
You hear that?

214
00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.780
[USOPP]
That's not what I mean!

215
00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.710
I wanna be a great warrior.

216
00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.280
I wanna be brave
and proud like you

217
00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.250
and the others from Elbaph.

218
00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.360
[laughs]

219
00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.930
I see.

220
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.260
You know, in Elbaph,
even though our lifespans

221
00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:47.520
are longer than yours are,
we still think about

222
00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.740
how we will die.

223
00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.610
We know everything
we have and everything

224
00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:55.480
we are will one day cease
to exist, like everything else.

225
00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:58.440
But it is worth it to die
a true warrior of Elbaph,

226
00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.450
without sacrificing
your pride.

227
00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.810
That is what we call
dying with honor.

228
00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.580
To die such a great death

229
00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:06.760
would be an
everlasting treasure.

230
00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:09.630
It's what we seek in Elbaph.

231
00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.590
So pride is your treasure.

232
00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.260
That's great!

233
00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.700
I've decided to learn from you!

234
00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:17.630
From now on,
I'll call you Master!

235
00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.800
[BROGY]
Huh?

236
00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:22.340
[DORRY groans]

237
00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.770
[gasps]

238
00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.780
[DORRY groans]

239
00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.680
[gasps]

240
00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.520
[screams]

241
00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:32.350
[DORRY groans]

242
00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:36.290
[LUFFY, VIVI gasp]

243
00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.260
Old giant guy!

244
00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.800
[LUFFY]
What's going on?

245
00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.700
Why did it explode?

246
00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.500
That was the same
alcohol we had with us

247
00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:48.360
on the ship, wasn't it?

248
00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.130
[DORRY groans]

249
00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.700
[VIVI]
It exploded in his stomach!

250
00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.110
The other giant must
have booby trapped it!

251
00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.940
Hold it! Were you
even watching them?!

252
00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.640
They fight their
duels honorably!

253
00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:01.510
No way he'd do that!

254
00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.960
All right, then who did do it?

255
00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:10.600
You strangers.

256
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.890
[DORRY growls]
It wasn't Brogy.

257
00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.760
No way...

258
00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.200
No warrior of Elbaph
would dare. So...

259
00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:23.350
Who else is there to suspect
on this island then...

260
00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.410
...besides you?

261
00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:26.420
[KAROO screams]

262
00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:27.650
Let's get out of here!

263
00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.750
There's no use talking
to him right now.

264
00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.390
I doubt running
would do us any good.

265
00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:35.290
Hold on to this and stay back.

266
00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:38.460
You're going to... fight Dorry?

267
00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:40.260
[panting]

268
00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.460
[knuckles crack]

269
00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.500
Yeah. I don't want to,

270
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.400
but we have to settle this.

271
00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.820
Don't do it, you guys! Stop it!

272
00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.620
Dorry, please just listen to me!

273
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.890
We don't know anything about
the explosives in the barrels,

274
00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.160
I promise! We wouldn't do that.

275
00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:03.090
You can't be in any shape to
fight right now, so please stop!

276
00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.150
Right.

277
00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:09.720
Why should I believe you liars?!

278
00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.750
[yells]

279
00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.160
[gasps]

280
00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.090
[groans]

281
00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:17.360
[LUFFY grunts]

282
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:21.100
[LUFFY yells]

283
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.550
All right, then, Gum-Gum...

284
00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.170
[LUFFY grunts]

285
00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:35.270
[yells]

286
00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.780
[groans]

287
00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:43.200
Gum-Gum...

288
00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.370
[DORRY panting]

289
00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:53.640
[LUFFY]
Sorry.

290
00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.070
...Rocket!

291
00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.080
[DORRY groans]

292
00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.540
[LUFFY growls]

293
00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.910
[screams]

294
00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.550
– [DORRY groans]
– [LUFFY yells]

295
00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.580
[DORRY growls]

296
00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.820
[LUFFY gasps]

297
00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.080
[gasps]

298
00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:24.090
[DORRY gags, coughs]

299
00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.460
[VIVI]
No! Luffy!

300
00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.760
I see now.

301
00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:28.930
[coughs]

302
00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:31.350
...one of the devil fruits!

303
00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.310
– ...him.
– [gasps]

304
00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.350
I don't know what else to do.

305
00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:46.040
[panting]

306
00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:53.550
[panting]

307
00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.830
[VIVI]
Luffy! Are you all right?

308
00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.230
How is he?

309
00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.630
[VIVI]
He should be okay.

310
00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:05.560
I guess you were
right about fighting.

311
00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:09.100
He's certainly a lot calmer now.

312
00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:10.970
[LUFFY]
Well, I'm not!

313
00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:14.150
The old guy was right
about one thing, anyway.

314
00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.580
The other giant would never
do anything like this.

315
00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.820
But I know that our friends
wouldn't do it either.

316
00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:21.190
They aren't like that.

317
00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:23.290
Yeah. Then who?

318
00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:28.480
[LUFFY]
There must be
somebody else on this island.

319
00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.110
[MR. 3]
The key to winning any game

320
00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.510
is to know your opponent's
state of mind.

321
00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:41.340
For now, we have succeeded
in confusing our enemy.

322
00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.700
They are no doubt wondering
about the mysterious bomb

323
00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:45.380
that we delivered.

324
00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:49.350
And about the identity
of their invisible enemy.

325
00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:50.190
Our first target

326
00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:52.580
was the long-bearded
giant, Dorry.

327
00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.710
I knew, of course, that it
would be nearly impossible

328
00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.190
to finish him off,

329
00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:58.210
but the damage done to
his stomach by the bomb

330
00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.390
must have been considerable.

331
00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.500
Now...

332
00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:04.540
We can sit here enjoying
our tea while relaxing...

333
00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:07.530
...and wait for the
next duel to start.

334
00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.590
So we stay in the
background and let the giant

335
00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.270
kill off the injured one?

336
00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.630
[MR. 3 chuckles]
Yes, that's exactly right.

337
00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.930
That's certainly
an indirect method.

338
00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.730
[MR. 3]
Again, you have
to consider your enemy.

339
00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.320
Warriors like these two
operate in much the same way

340
00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:22.300
as wild boars.

341
00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.400
They can be intimidating
in a head-on fight,

342
00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:25.600
but they don't have

343
00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:28.270
the brains to think beyond
their immediate circumstance.

344
00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.840
So why bother going
after them directly

345
00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.820
when you have the intelligence
to destroy them indirectly?

346
00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.450
[MR. 3 chuckles]

347
00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.110
Seriously...

348
00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:50.570
[MR. 3]
Why can't you
just get the tea yourself,

349
00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.490
Miss Golden Week?

350
00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.190
[MR. 5]
And just what
are we supposed to do

351
00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:55.660
with the Straw Hat Gang?

352
00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.330
Straw Hat Gang...?

353
00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.670
Oh, you're talking
about the little brats

354
00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.730
who found out
the Boss's secrets.

355
00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.500
We can start by luring
them out one by one.

356
00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.650
The order doesn't matter really.

357
00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:10.520
Let's start with the one
closest to my tea set.

358
00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.170
I have a personal
motto, you know:

359
00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:15.020
And that is, "Big crimes
via cheap tricks."

360
00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.990
[laughs]

361
00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:19.180
There are plenty of good
ways to defeat any enemy...

362
00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:21.180
all without fighting.

363
00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.320
[rumbling, explosions]

364
00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.350
[gasps]

365
00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.020
That's their signal... isn't it?

366
00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:35.550
[BROGY]
Well, there's the signal.

367
00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.570
It's really been active today.

368
00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:40.360
You're really going?

369
00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:44.000
But your wounds from the
last battle haven't healed!

370
00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:48.500
Please! Dorry can't be
doing any better than me!

371
00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.690
[Brogy laughs]

372
00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:53.260
A few scratches won't
take me out of a duel!

373
00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:57.010
That would surely be a poor
excuse for a brave warrior.

374
00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.070
[laughs]

375
00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:04.140
[pants]

376
00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.940
[LUFFY]
Wait, giant guy!

377
00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:06.940
Don't!

378
00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.140
[VIVI]
You can't fight,
Dorry! You need to rest!

379
00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.400
You'll die if you
push yourself too hard!

380
00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:17.220
I will fight... I am Dorry...

381
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.550
I will... [sputtters]

382
00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:22.820
...fight... for Elbaph's
pride and die as a warrior.

383
00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:28.490
Now, Master Brogy,
go and show this guy!

384
00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:29.390
[laughs]

385
00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:33.540
[Usopp mimics Brogy]

386
00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.440
You bet, Usopp!

387
00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.710
I'm gonna beat him
for sure this time.

388
00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.440
He hasn't got a chance.

389
00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.780
[USOPP]
Go get him,
you great warrior of Elbaph!

390
00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.620
The mighty Brogy always
defeats his opponent!

391
00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:46.650
– [Brogy laughs]
– [USOPP] You can do it, Brogy!

392
00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:48.690
You're the mightiest
warrior in the world!

393
00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.620
You can destroy him any day!

394
00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.120
You're gonna crush him!

395
00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:53.660
Go, Warrior Brogy!

396
00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.360
– Fight like the...
– [NAMI] Why does he continue

397
00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.460
this pointless fight?

398
00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.620
How can you say something
like this is pointless?!

399
00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.700
Brogy is a brave warrior,
just like I'm gonna be someday!

400
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.470
You have no right to
say anything, you idiot!

401
00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:04.140
– If you weren't a girl...
– [NAMI] Well now we can

402
00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:05.240
think about getting
back to the ship.

403
00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.370
Waiting for a year...

404
00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:09.420
There's no freakin' way.
It's completely unacceptable.

405
00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:10.850
We need to get everyone
back on the ship

406
00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:11.890
and come up with a plan.

407
00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.630
[USOPP]
Now hold on a second!

408
00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:17.050
I for one don't think
we stand a chance

409
00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.750
in a fight against dinosaurs!

410
00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.420
Cutting through the jungle
in order to get back

411
00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:23.330
to the Merry won't do us
much good if we get killed

412
00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:24.490
on the way, will it?

413
00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:26.760
What happened to all that
"brave warrior of the sea"

414
00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.530
stuff you've been
going on about?

415
00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:30.470
I said that someday
I would be a brave warrior

416
00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.600
of the sea. Besides, even
a brave warrior has to have

417
00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.870
enough sense not to
get himself killed.

418
00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.540
[NAMI]
We don't have a choice here.

419
00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:39.550
Luffy's group is over at
the other giant's place.

420
00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:41.700
We should probably
head that way first.

421
00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:42.800
Nami, listen.

422
00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.370
Even if I should lose everything
someday, and I must face

423
00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:48.650
a horribly tragic death...
alone on a deserted island...

424
00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.560
I, will proudly say this
about how I have lived:

425
00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:52.210
I am Captain Usopp,

426
00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:56.410
and know that I have been a
great, brave warrior of the sea!

427
00:21:58.130 --> 00:21:59.170
[NAMI]
Yeah, yeah.

428
00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:01.890
But for now, do you
think you could just

429
00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.750
try to be a dependable warrior?

430
00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:05.890
Right. Let's go.

431
00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:11.560
[rumbling]

432
00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:15.340
Come on! What are you doing?

433
00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:16.840
– Get this rock off me!
– [DORRY] It can't be

434
00:22:16.840 --> 00:22:18.110
– Get this rock off me!
– helped now.

435
00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:23.850
It's been over a century...

436
00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:29.290
...since we started
the battle... this duel.

437
00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:33.790
Injured or not,
I cannot allow myself

438
00:22:33.820 --> 00:22:35.800
to run away from this fight.

439
00:22:35.800 --> 00:22:39.120
To do so would be like running
from the title of warrior.

440
00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.920
And if I was no longer
a warrior of Elbaph,

441
00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:45.200
then I would no longer
know who I am.

442
00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:51.000
[DORRY]
I'm sorry I suspected
you of causing the explosion.

443
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.940
I now know that
this was a judgment.

444
00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:56.900
[DORRY]
A judgment from Elbaph...

445
00:22:56.900 --> 00:22:59.070
The god of war.

446
00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:01.230
I didn't have the
god's protection...

447
00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:03.360
...and that is all.

448
00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:07.790
Listen to me: Gods and
protection and judgments

449
00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:10.290
have nothing to do
with what's going on!

450
00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:13.800
If a god told you to just
run off and die, would you?!

451
00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.250
Someone has interfered
with your duel!

452
00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:19.520
And a duel that's
been interfered with

453
00:23:19.550 --> 00:23:21.450
isn't a fair fight anymore!

454
00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:23.220
Isn't that right?

455
00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:26.220
[DORRY]
Silence.

456
00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:27.870
What can you know about this?

457
00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.280
You're a human who can't have
been living on this earth

458
00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:31.580
for more than two decades.

459
00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:34.150
How can you possibly
hope to understand

460
00:23:34.190 --> 00:23:36.420
the ways of the
warriors of Elbaph?

461
00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:37.990
[LUFFY]
Who cares about that stuff?!

462
00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:40.760
Now get this damn thing off me!

463
00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:43.400
Hey! Old guy! Listen to me!

464
00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:45.400
Move this rock already! Come on!

465
00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:46.670
Come back here!

466
00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:49.320
You can't leave me
trapped like this!

467
00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:58.140
[Brogy laughs]
Dorry, how was your drink?

468
00:23:58.140 --> 00:24:01.140
Hit the spot, didn't it?

469
00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:04.040
Yes. It tasted almost godly.

470
00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.980
[laughs]
Well, I'm glad
that you enjoyed it.

471
00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:09.230
Let's go!

472
00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:10.920
[Brogy yells]

473
00:24:11.490 --> 00:24:12.650
[laughs]

474
00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:14.870
[Brogy growls]

475
00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:16.100
[yells]

476
00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:20.400
What's... wrong?
You... seem... weak.

477
00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:23.230
[DORRY]
Don't count on it.

478
00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:24.830
I'm as strong as ever.

479
00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:28.540
[Luffy growling]

480
00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:31.320
[LUFFY]
Move, you stupid rock! Come on!

481
00:24:32.480 --> 00:24:33.480
Of course.

482
00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:36.150
Just when I meet a great
warrior, this happens!

483
00:24:36.150 --> 00:24:38.990
Just calm down.

484
00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:41.140
[VIVI]
I don't understand
why he's so upset

485
00:24:41.170 --> 00:24:42.760
over someone that he just met.

486
00:24:42.760 --> 00:24:44.790
He sure doesn't seem much
like a hardened criminal

487
00:24:44.830 --> 00:24:47.190
with a bounty on his head.

488
00:24:47.190 --> 00:24:49.930
Who was it?! Who would
dare to interfere?

489
00:24:49.930 --> 00:24:51.670
I'll kill them!

490
00:24:53.730 --> 00:24:55.670
Hey, Luffy...

491
00:24:55.670 --> 00:24:57.190
Karoo's missing!

492
00:24:58.010 --> 00:25:04.010
[footsteps]

493
00:25:05.230 --> 00:25:06.670
This isn't good.

494
00:25:06.670 --> 00:25:08.170
I'm lost.

495
00:25:08.170 --> 00:25:09.160
This tree looks familiar,

496
00:25:09.190 --> 00:25:11.470
but it's kinda hard
to tell in this place.

497
00:25:11.470 --> 00:25:13.130
I think I was supposed to
take a left at the tree

498
00:25:13.170 --> 00:25:15.280
wrapped in vines.

499
00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:19.360
[ZORO]
Oh. Hey, Nami, it's you!

500
00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:21.000
Seems I got lost.

501
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:22.660
Looks like you got
some pretty good timing.

502
00:25:22.660 --> 00:25:24.490
I wasn't sure what
I was gonna do.

503
00:25:24.490 --> 00:25:28.660
So what are you doin'
in this area anyway, huh?

504
00:25:29.390 --> 00:25:31.460
Uh... Nami?

505
00:25:32.890 --> 00:25:35.020
[Usopp screams]

506
00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:37.160
Oh, crap, it's another dinosaur!

507
00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:38.620
Get away, get away,
get away, get away,

508
00:25:38.650 --> 00:25:40.000
get away, get away!

509
00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:43.870
Usopp, wait up!

510
00:25:43.870 --> 00:25:48.910
[panting]

511
00:25:48.910 --> 00:25:50.540
Luffy!

512
00:25:50.540 --> 00:25:52.580
[NAMI]
Boy, is it a relief to see you!

513
00:25:52.580 --> 00:25:54.440
So what are you
doing here, anyway?

514
00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:01.910
[gasps, yelps]

515
00:26:02.910 --> 00:26:04.780
[Usopp screaming]

516
00:26:07.920 --> 00:26:09.320
[USOPP]
Uh, Nami?

517
00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:10.820
[dinosaurs squawking]

518
00:26:20.350 --> 00:26:23.810
[USOPP]
Nami! Nami! Nami! Nami!

519
00:26:24.980 --> 00:26:26.780
Where did she go?!

520
00:26:26.980 --> 00:26:28.180
Luffy!

521
00:26:36.170 --> 00:26:39.740
The scope of this planet's so vast and so grand

522
00:26:39.700 --> 00:26:43.090
That if treasure's out there, well where do you start?

523
00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:46.380
Keep your wits about you, don’t leave it to chance

524
00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:50.480
Yeah play it smart but don’t forget
that in the end you’re still rolling the dice

525
00:26:52.520 --> 00:26:53.650
And that's why...

526
00:26:56.390 --> 00:26:59.680
If someone gets in our way, well who cares?

527
00:26:59.730 --> 00:27:03.070
If someone’s running their mouth, well who cares?

528
00:27:03.050 --> 00:27:08.560
Let's sail out, yeah we'll tell all the losers here "bon voyage"

529
00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:10.250
Get lost and stay

530
00:27:10.010 --> 00:27:16.370
Cause even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna get it done

531
00:27:16.380 --> 00:27:22.950
The more impossible the impressive, reach for the stars

532
00:27:23.060 --> 00:27:29.670
Yeah, even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna take you on

533
00:27:29.700 --> 00:27:36.340
If we can sail across this vast sea we’ll find a paradise

534
00:27:36.690 --> 00:27:42.050
Go ahead and give it your best,
next time you look out your telescope

535
00:27:41.810 --> 00:27:43.850
You’ll find you’re one step closer
